# Implement T3 service supervision diagnostics and repair

## Context

Design: `.collab/design/2026-10-19-c2c-t3-external-connector.md`.
Pending planned work. During execution follow bl-fix-many: read the full ticket, verify blockers, commit the claim, work in an isolated worktree, review/fix, run the c2c gates on build boxes, merge and close. No T3 source changes. Tests use x-p35/x-tuf, never the workstation's full suite. Actual just bi and service installation wait for the current candidate's successful P9.M2.E1.T001 buildbox gate.

## Requirements

- Implement c2c t3 service in foreground, service install to write/enable/start the owned user-systemd unit, service doctor read-only, and service repair conservative. Expose pair/list/status and documented operator-mode control.
- Explicit executable and T3-home paths in the unit; no dependence on interactive shell PATH. Verify the process and connector readiness, not just systemctl exit status.
- Repair only owned permission, unit, runtime-cache and alias/lease drift under the proper lock/control path. Never replace OAuth tokens, delete queued mail, remove a live lock or steal foreign routes.
- Missing auth/runtime/relay reports partial health accurately with actionable commands. T3 process restart triggers transport recovery; expired auth requires explicit re-pair.
- Add dry-run repair and safe service stop/uninstall semantics. User-owned configuration is preserved.
- Include recovery in this single service: default enabled on verified compatible versions, explicit recovery-disable setting, and doctor evidence/hold/cadence/submission state. A messaging-ready process must not conceal an unsupported or failing monitor.
- This task implements and fixture-tests the installer; it does not run just bi or deploy the unit. Actual installation waits for P9.M2.E1.T001 and is performed in P9.M2.E1.T002.
- Implement optional C2C_VALIDATION_RECEIPT enforcement in the existing install guard: inside the install flock, after generators/build and before copies, compare the clean commit/tree, toolchain/dependencies and all eight prepared artifact hashes with the preserved successful gate manifest. Reject malformed/mismatched supplied receipts without partial copying. Preserve ordinary receipt-free installs; this rollout must supply the receipt. Keep existing ancestry guard enabled.

## Acceptance Criteria

- Tests cover systemd present/absent, idempotent install, stale executable/PID, competing foreground instance, missing/revoked token, malformed config and repair against live owner.
- Doctor is read-only and returns structured redacted health including queue age, scan age, permission ceiling and uncertain entries.
- Installer fixture tests prove enable-and-start behavior without modifying T3. Uninstall touches only manifest/owned artifacts and retains mail/state by default.
- Each command has accurate help and operational documentation.
- Guard fixture tests mutate source/generated output/artifact/receipt between validation and copy and prove that install is refused. Comparing newly built files only with newly installed files must not bypass the original PASS manifest.

## Lane

After T005/T006/T009. CLI registry and shared service edits are one serialized integration lane. Install and doctor cover model-availability recovery inside the same process.
